# __MODULE__

A [Facet Architecture](https://fct.dev) app. The page is a
**Playground** (the base canvas); your facets live in `facets/` and are
server-rendered, then updated live over SSE — no client framework, no API layer.

## Run

```sh
go run .
# open http://localhost:7373  (set FA_ADDR to change)
```

Click the heart: the browser POSTs to the single `/events` endpoint, the server
toggles state, re-renders the `LikeButton` facet, and pushes the swap back over
SSE. The client runtime just applies it — it holds no application logic.

## Develop

```sh
fct dev        # rebuilds and restarts on .fct change
```

## Layout

```
facets/        your facets (.fct)  — edit these
main.go        wiring: compile facets, handle events, serve the Playground
fct.toml       project config
```

> Pre-release: until `fct.dev` is published, point it at a local
> checkout:
>
> ```sh
> go mod edit -replace fct.dev=/path/to/facet
> ```
